 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 4 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.16.1062) - AMD Ryzen 7 9700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.16 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using a **floating Shader Editor**, spawning a context tooltip (by using RMB on a `.gdshader` file for example) **spawns the context on the Monitor that the main Godot Engine Window is currently on, and not the monitor that the Shader Editor is currently on.**\n\n<img width=\"1201\" height=\"801\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/07fa443b-213d-495b-8537-c80b81f044dc\" />\n\n_The white area on the left is the Main Monitor, the Shader Editor is on a secondary monitor in Portrait mode_\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the Shader Editor\n2. Make it floating and move it to a different Monitor from the main Godot Engine Window\n3. Spawn a tooltip by right-clicking the `.gdshader` file in the list\n4. The tooltip will spawn on the edge of the Monitor that has the Godot Engine Window\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received